            <div xml:id="d1088">

                <pb facs="1050" n="1038" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.00/235: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-20T07:00:00+02:00">November 20,
                            1943—7 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2128. My voluntary comment on London’s 8050, November 18, 7 p.m., repeated here
                    is that the expedient apparently under consideration is immoral in concept and
                    pernicious in effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
